lesson: 250
title: Distances out and about
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A kilometre is 1000 metres. Going somewhere and back means covering the distance twice.
explain: To find the whole walk in metres, turn the kilometres into metres, double them for the way back, and add any extra distance walked there.
explain: 2 km to the park and back is 2 × 2000 = 4000 m; with 3 laps of 250 m round the park the walk is 4000 + 750 = 4750 m.
vars: a=name b=name d=1..4 k=2..6 c=4..10 z=2..9
let: r = c * 50
answer: 2 * d * 1000 + k * r
exercise: {a} walks {d} km to the park and back home again. At the park {a.he} runs {k} laps of a {r} m track. How many metres does {a.he} cover in all?
exercise: The pool is {d} km from {a}'s house. {a} cycles there and back, and while there {a.he} walks {k} times round the {r} m path outside the pool. How many metres does {a.he} travel altogether?
exercise: {a} jogs {d} km to the beach and back. At the beach {a.he} walks {k} times round a {r} m sandcastle trail. How many metres is the whole outing?
exercise: A school trip goes {d} km to the farm and returns the same way. On the farm the class walks {k} times round a {r} m field. How many metres do they walk?
exercise: {a} walks the dog {d} km to the woods and back and throws a ball along a {r} m trail {k} times, running the trail each time. How many metres does {a} cover?
exercise: walked {d} k to the park n back, plus {k} laps of the {r} m loop. how many metres all up
exercise: {a} went {d} km to nan's and back, then {k+1}, no sorry {k} laps of the {r} m track. metres total?
exercise: me and {b} biked {d} km to the lake and home, did {k} rounds of the {r} m path, saw a heron lol. how far in metres
exercise: {b} reckons {d} km there and back plus {k} laps of {r} m is {d*1000+k*r} m. forgot the way back didn't she? how many metres really
exercise: {d} km to the shops and back, plus {k} laps of {r} m round the car park looking for mum lol. metres?
exercise: {a} ran {d} km to the oval and back, and did {k} laps of {r} m there. total metres
test: How many metres in all does {a} cover by walking {d} km out to a lake, going round its {r} m shore path {k} times, and walking {d} km home?
test: The library is {d} km away. {a} walks there, then {k} times round the {r} m garden beside it, then home the same way. Give the total distance in metres.
test: {a} cycles {d} km to the sports ground and back. There {a.he} does {k} laps of a {r} m track while {b} does {z} laps. How many metres does {a} cover?
test: The zoo is {d} km from home, and {a} walks there and back; inside, {a} walks a {r} m loop {k} times. What distance, in metres, does {a.he} walk that day?
test: {d}km to school n back plus {k} laps of {r}m at PE, metres?
test: walked {d} km there, {d} km home, {k} goes round the {r} m trail. metres altogether eh
exam: Determine, in metres, the aggregate distance traversed by {a}, who proceeds {d.words} kilometres to a park, completes {k.words} circuits of a {r} m track, and returns by the same route.
exam: It is given that a pupil travels {d} km to a destination and subsequently returns by the identical route, having in the interim completed {k} laps of {r} metres. Ascertain the total distance in metres.
exam: A journey of {d} km in each direction having been undertaken, together with {k} circuits of a path measuring {r} m, state the whole distance covered, expressed in metres.
exam: Whereas {a} walks {d} km to the woods, {k} times round a trail of {r} m, and {d} km home, compute the total distance walked in metres.
exercise: Since Mum was let go, the family walks everywhere. {a} walks {d} km to the park and back, and there {a.he} runs {k} laps of a {r} m track. How many metres does {a.he} cover in all?
exercise: the bloody bus is experiencing delays again, useless, so {a} legs it {d} km to school and {d} km home, plus {k} laps of the {r} m track in PE. how many metres is that?
test: {a}'s old dog was put to sleep, so {a} now walks the route alone: {d} km to the river and {d} km home, with {k} rounds of the {r} m field on the way. How far is that in metres?
